WEBVTT

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.200
How many enemy mechs?

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.440
How many are left?

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.980
Kobayashi's severely damaged!

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:17.740
We've lost contact with Yamamoto, too!

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.920
What's going on? Dammit!

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.350
G-Ghost?

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:12.960
Someday, in this space deprived of hope,
kono takaki mubou no kuu de itsuka

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.630
you'll kneel of your own will.
sono ishi wa hiza wo tateru

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.850
break up foreordination

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:33.730
Was that flame an illusion or a friend?
fake ano hi wa nakama ka

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:38.440
Am I to venture into the darkness?
susumu beki wa yami ka

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:47.740
You'll find nameless emotions beyond the protruding knife.
knife tsukitateta saki ni shoutai no mienu kanjou

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.580
I can't let this end here yet.
ima wa mada koko de owarenai

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:58.710
I need to get ready to survive.
naraba ikiru junbi wo shiro yo

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:04.010
The passion in my heart only burns hotter.
uzu takaku tsumiageteku netsujou

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:07.510
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:08.970
wake up your tough intention

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:09.930
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:14.180
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:20.820
I'll show you what I've got, bit by bit,
hitotsu zutsu tashikamete yaru kara

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.360
so bring it on.
kakattekoi

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.870
break up foreordination

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:42.500
Ghost

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.510
Our ace recon unit was taken out, huh?

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:49.760
It's out of ammo.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.510
They fired down to their last round.

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:55.270
How many times has this happened?

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:58.120
And all with veteran troops...

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.280
Senpai, what do you think?

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:11.560
It looks like everyone was running around terrified before they were killed.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:13.680
Yeah.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.020
What kind of attack was it?

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:21.290
From the look of the remains, it was probably a Trail Krieger.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.250
The enemy's new model?

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.300
No way.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:30.120
But someday, the Seiran and Argevollen will be obsolete.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:35.240
They say that by the time a weapon is out of development and used in battle,

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.100
it's already obsolete.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:41.880
This is...

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:46.230
Captain, you don't think it was really...

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:47.660
The Ghost?

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:59.250
Okay, okay!

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.500
Just like that, slowly!

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.580
Orbay, Seamoccia, Nishizamahara,

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.690
Knieven, and Kitazamahara.

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:11.510
The enemy has attacked repeatedly in this area.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.510
The Ghost...?

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:19.520
Sergeant Major Suzushiro, please don't use that name in front of the troops.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.760
Thanks. I'll be careful.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:28.030
The common point in all the enemy attacks is that they wiped everything out.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.660
There were no survivors on any battlefield.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:34.280
They don't want to leave any witnesses, possibly?

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:36.660
That's likely the case.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.930
In order to combat this unknown enemy,

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.360
we're deploying multiple units.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:47.680
The fact that Independent Unit 8 was deployed here, to Kitazamahara,

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:52.760
means that command is well aware of how important this base is.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.360
Either that, or the enemy has chosen isolated, unimportant locations

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.680
to test its new weapons.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:07.190
A local, tactical victory does not equal a greater, strategic victory.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.200
What do you think will happen in this war?

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.150
The stronger side will win, I suppose.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:20.450
The captain does have an authoritarian streak in him, that's for sure.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:23.040
You didn't have to say that.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.600
We're changing our formation shifts.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.580
Get to work immediately.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:41.870
I really should tell him that I heard what happened to his sister.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.610
So the Seiran can do that.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.310
Tokimune!

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:50.360
What?

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:53.110
Um...

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:57.720
I just got a message that a new update arrived for Argevollen's control plugin.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.000
Check it out before I run the install.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.420
Okay.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.460
A new model? Now?

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:14.400
It's Brigadier General Zarl's idea.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:15.940
We can't turn it down.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:18.950
Between training the pilot and working out logistics,

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.470
the pressure it'll put on us will be no laughing matter.

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:26.480
We need shock treatment to break this stalemate.

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:31.680
There are rumors that its developers, Fordergrunt Inc., have been

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:34.240
throwing around bribe money to get it here.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.880
Don't say anything reckless.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.730
Intelligence already has its eyes on us.

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:40.490
Right.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:43.520
I don't know what Zarl is thinking,

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:46.720
but he probably thinks that

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:49.570
since he got us this new model before Intelligence could, we owe him one.

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:52.000
So let him think that.

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.740
Don't forget, Garp.

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:07.590
It's important to make both Zarl and Intelligence underestimate us.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:08.350
Yes, sir.

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:10.890
Everything is for the motherland.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:27.040
What do you think of the food?

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:28.410
Quantity over quality.

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:33.190
The fancy stuff here won't fill my stomach.

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:39.880
This is Ingelmia's new model.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:43.080
I don't like beating around the bush.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.350
You know that, right?

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:48.520
What do you want? An additional order?

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:50.850
That's exactly right.

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:55.330
It's not that I don't understand your position.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:58.610
Wasn't Kybernes technology used in this?

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:01.230
A coincidence, nothing more.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:03.620
And there's no such thing as borders when it comes to technology.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:06.390
You have an answer for everything, don't you?

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:08.250
What happened with that other matter?

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.620
What do you mean?

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:13.420
What could I possibly mean besides the U-Link?

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:14.720
Don't try to hide it.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.230
There is no problem.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:18.380
Trust our company's technology.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:22.890
You said the same thing with Cape Sagara.

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:26.640
Cape Sagara?

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:34.860
You will work in a two-shift system of twelve-hour shifts

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:39.150
to prepare for the attack by the enemy's new Trail Krieger.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:44.600
From 2000 this evening to 0800 tomorrow morning,

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:47.540
Private Susumu and Private Portman will be on duty.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:50.900
Private Susumu's been here longer, so he'll be in charge.

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:51.870
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:56.570
After 0800, Corporal Juliano and Sergeant Appleton will be on duty.

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:57.630
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:57.630 --> 00:09:04.920
We'll also ask Hazaford-san to be on night duty to help with Argevollen.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.140
Understood.

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:07.830
Any questions?

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:10.890
Captain?

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:16.190
Command wants it captured, but we don't know what the enemy's new model can do.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:19.530
You have permission to destroy it if you feel the situation requires it.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.070
Yes, sir!

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:44.720
Okay!

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:53.180
Where's Portman-san?

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:54.460
The galley.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.960
She asked the head cook if she could make dinner.

00:09:57.960 --> 00:09:58.860
Huh?

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.380
What do you mean, "huh"?

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:04.430
It's just a little surprising, that's all.

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:10.330
Is the heater on?

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:11.560
Isn't it a little cold?

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.180
This is a desert, after all.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:15.910
There's probably a blanket around here somewhere.

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.040
Hey, um...

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:30.430
What? I looked at the plugin.

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:32.390
Not that...

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:37.100
You and Argevollen have been getting along well lately, huh?

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:40.810
The Linkage Depth numbers have been going up.

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:44.500
It makes me proud to be the engineer in charge.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.940
What? That's kind of creepy.

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:53.020
I heard, a while back.

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:54.250
Heard what?

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.540
About your, um...

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.670
About your sister and Captain Samonji.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.630
I wasn't trying to listen!

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:06.890
I just happened to hear Suzushiro-san talking.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.460
It's true.

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.680
How much did you hear?

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:16.930
That your sister and Samonji-san got to be, um... close.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:22.400
And that they were together when your sister died.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:23.750
That's all of it.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:25.440
Yeah.

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:29.760
I thought you were acting weird lately.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:33.460
Well, it's a personal matter...

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.450
Just pretend you don't know anything about it.

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.270
I can't do that.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.360
Well, you don't have to worry about it.

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:46.330
The military kept insisting my sister's death was an accident.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.240
They wouldn't tell me anything.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:53.470
But after talking with Suzushiro-san, I finally found out.

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:55.140
So it's okay now.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:58.720
You're sure it's okay?

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:00.760
Not if you say it like that.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:01.660
Right?

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:02.920
But it's okay.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:04.420
Which is it?

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:08.240
I'm not sure how to say it, but...

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:13.240
Even if I complain, things won't go back to the way they were.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.680
Dinner's ready.

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:27.630
It's been a week.

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:30.270
There's no sign of the Ghost.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:33.140
Maybe it went to heaven?

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:35.100
That'd be great.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.640
Of course it didn't. That's idiotic!

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:41.550
If it could be beaten that easily, none of us would have a problem.

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:42.770
Let's go.

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:45.650
It was just a joke...

00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:15.720
Saber-1 to Arrowhead!

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:17.650
We are in combat with the enemy!

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:18.930
Requesting immediate reinforcements!

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:20.680
Arrowhead, come in!

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:23.440
Saber-1 is in combat with Ingelmia Trail Kriegers!

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:30.270
Saber-1, this is Arrowhead!

00:13:30.270 --> 00:13:31.770
Come in, Saber-1!

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:09.340
All forces arriving in position.

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:10.570
Get Lt. Samonji on the line.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:12.790
Lt. Samonji, on screen.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:14.820
What is it?

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:18.070
What's going on with your new model?

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:20.070
It's ready.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:21.380
Send it to the front.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:23.150
I want constant updates.

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:24.580
Yes, sir.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.720
The enemy wiped out one of our patrol units,

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:41.970
and is heading toward us from bearing 1-2-5.

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:43.470
Roger!

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:47.850
Silfy and Lorenz's Seirans are ready to go.

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:54.620
Seiran 1 and Seiran 2 will rendezvous with Argevollen and Seiran 3.

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:55.490
Roger.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.660
It's heading straight for us?

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:14.980
What's happening on the front lines?

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:15.780
Hurry up and deal with it!

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:16.470
Yes, sir!

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:18.590
No tricks, huh?

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:20.530
Be careful, you two.

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:21.420
Yes, ma'am!

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:24.350
It's moving as fast as Argevollen, if not faster.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:28.450
Recalculate the predicted encounter point and send it to the pilots.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:29.410
Yes, sir!

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:31.580
Captain Amagi.

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:32.420
What?

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:34.930
We should deploy more forward squads.

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:36.480
I'm in command here!

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:37.610
Just give me the information!

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:38.870
Yes, sir.

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:51.200
That's the fastest Ingelmian unit I've ever seen.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:52.660
Be careful. It's coming!

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:53.250
Right!

00:15:58.010 --> 00:15:59.140
Above you!

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:27.300
This thing...

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:29.660
Namie!

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:31.020
I'm all right!

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:32.750
Namie unit, mind your distance.

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:33.780
Roger!

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:37.100
Captain Amagi, deploy the base's Trail Krieger squads.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:38.490
I know!

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:41.420
Silfy, Lorenz, fall back and secure a position.

00:16:41.420 --> 00:16:42.180
Roger.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:42.680
Right!

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.690
So this is the power of the new model?

00:16:58.690 --> 00:16:59.690
No!

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:05.000
Silfy! Lorenz!

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:06.630
They broke past Tokimune and Namie!

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:09.950
Enemy bombardment!

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.530
Well, this is a problem.

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:53.080
Damn it!

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:54.570
Hit him! Hit him!

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:55.580
Senpai...

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:16.350
What's this?

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:19.680
Linkage Depth 70...

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:22.360
75, 80...

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:33.410
Have them send in their reports so we can concentrate fire!

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:35.160
What are you doing?!

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:42.380
Ghost...

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:53.890
Damn you!

00:19:24.250 --> 00:19:25.510
Namie!

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.210
Tokimune!

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:23.580
Are you okay, Tokimune?

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:24.980
Namie-chan, are you hurt?

00:20:24.980 --> 00:20:26.810
No, I'm fine.

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:47.010
That thing was...

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:51.590
What happened with that other problem?

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:55.350
No signs of it for the moment.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.820
Excellent.

00:20:56.820 --> 00:21:02.350
Tell Kybernes and Fordergrunt to move the plan to the next stage.

00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:06.390
It's critical that we begin mass production

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:09.230
before the issues with NR Syndrome begin to manifest.

00:21:09.230 --> 00:21:13.240
Make sure that both companies understand this.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:21.280
Welcome back, Second Lieutenant Richthofen.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:23.060
Second Lieutenant Roderick.

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:26.830
The latency in the targeting system hasn't been improved.

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:28.910
It needs tuning immediately.

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:32.510
But the mechanics say this is the best they can do right now.

00:21:32.510 --> 00:21:36.510
Sturm Alpha must be perfected at once.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:39.130
I'll see to it immediately.

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:46.670
About our next target...

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:47.960
I'm changing the target.

00:21:47.960 --> 00:21:48.650
Sir?

00:21:48.650 --> 00:21:50.490
I found it.

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:52.150
<i>Argevollen!</i>

00:21:59.990 --> 00:22:13.300
We gaze into each other's eyes, open our hearts.

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:19.510
A cycle of strength and weakness.

00:22:19.510 --> 00:22:26.140
Your eyes must have adjusted somewhat.

00:22:26.140 --> 00:22:32.820
Verbalize though I may,

00:22:32.820 --> 00:22:40.620
I remember that I can't

00:22:40.620 --> 00:22:47.250
rationalize everything

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:54.420
The world will change, as long as I remain courageous.

00:22:55.670 --> 00:23:02.430
The telepathy I wouldn't have discovered alone,

00:23:02.430 --> 00:23:08.560
leads me ahead, behind your dazzling silouette.

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:15.940
But even so, I'll keep my unwavering gaze on you;

00:23:15.940 --> 00:23:22.530
It'll reach you someday.

00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:39.380
Sturm
